    <values><field>Active__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:boolean">true</value></values><values><field>Advice__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">An agent reads field descriptions to decide what a field means and when to use it, so an empty description is a readiness gap. Write one or two plain sentences per field: what it holds, where the value comes from, and what it must not be used for.</value></values><values><field>Category__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">DQ</value></values><values><field>Check_Type__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Automated</value></values><values><field>Critical__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:boolean">false</value></values><values><field>Handler__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">FieldDescriptions</value></values><values><field>Level__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Implementation</value></values><values><field>Pass_Criteria__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">80% or more of custom grounding fields have a description or help text.</value></values><values><field>Question__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Checks whether the custom fields the agent grounds on have a description or help text. Agents use this metadata to work out what a field means.</value></values><values><field>Resources__c</field><value xsi:nil="true"/></values><values><field>Sort_Order__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:double">640</value></values><values><field>Topic__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">T7</value></values>
